<p>\(= ({@ev(a4*c4*x^2,simp)+ev(a4*d4*x,simp)+ ev(b4*c4*x,simp)+ev(b4*d4,simp)@})({@ev(e4*x+f4,simp)@})\) </p>
<p> \(=({@ev(expand((a4*x+b4)*(c4*x+d4)),simp)@}) ({@ev(e4*x+f4,simp)@})\)</p>
<p>\(= {@unary_minus_sort(ev(a4*c4*e4*x^3,simp) + ev(a4*c4*f4*x^2,simp) + ev((a4*d4+b4*c4)*e4*x^2,simp)+ev((a4*d4+b4*c4)*f4*x,simp)+ev(b4*d4*e4*x,simp) +ev(b4*d4*f4,simp) ) @}\)</p>
<p>\(= {@unary_minus_sort(ev(a4*c4*e4*x^3,simp) + ev(a4*c4*f4*x^2 + (a4*d4+b4*c4)*e4*x^2,simp) + +ev((a4*d4+b4*c4)*f4*x+b4*d4*e4*x,simp) +ev(b4*d4*f4,simp) ) @}.\)</p>
<p>Note that it doesn’t matter which two brackets we multiply out first. If we multiply out the second and third brackets first, we obtain the same final result: </p>
